  "discussion": "A small northwest swell will continue to fade today as a moderate north-northwest swell arrives. Surf along north and west-facing shores should build quickly today and top out near or slightly above seasonal average during the peak of the swell this afternoon into tonight, then slowly decline Saturday and Sunday as the dropping swell shifts more northerly. A smaller overlapping northwest swell arrives at the same time, which will bolster surf heights on Sunday. Both swells fade early next week. A new long-periond south swell will peak today, pushing surf along south-facing shores back above seasonal average through tonight. This swell will slowly decline Saturday through early next week. Surf along east-facing shores will gradually increase today as trade winds strengthen over the region. Expect some wrap from the moderate north-northwest swell Friday afternoon into Saturday. This swell along with developing rough trade wind swell will produce east shore surf above seasonal average Saturday through early next week.",
